### Page 12 of 18

```text
THE BLUE RAVEN BREWERY TEAM
April 20th, 2022
209 E. 1gth Street
Cheyenne, WY 82001
301-312-9471
support@blueravenbrewery.com
Mayor Collins and Members of the Cheyenne City Council
City of Cheyenne
2101 O’Neil Avenue
Cheyenne, WY 82001
Dear Mayor Collins and Members of the Cheyenne City Council,
We wish to come before you in the coming weeks to present our application to obtain a microbrewery license so that we
may operate as Blue Raven Brewery at the location formerly known as Danielmark’s Brewing Company, located at 209 E.
1gth Street in the downtown area. Our plans are to provide a safe and friendly environment for socialization for the whole
family, while fostering good relations with our neighbors, fellow community members, and visitors to Cheyenne. We will
carry on the tradition of providing a venue for charitable events, food live music, food trucks, trivia and game nights, so that
we may do our part in enhancing the entertainment offerings downtown.
To include one of the prior owners, all of the employees which worked at Danielmark’s have decided to stay on at Blue
Raven Brewery. Also, here are short backgrounds for each of the Blue Raven Brewery owners:
Ryan Willson has been the brewer at Danielmark’s for the past 3+ years with about 6 years of professional brewing
experience. Not only does he love living in Cheyenne and plans to stay indefinitely, his wife Sara, who was born and raised
in here, is an art teacher. Their roots in our community continue to grow every day with every beer imbibed and student
taught.
Kevin Tighe was born and raised in Cheyenne. He’s currently a fireman/paramedic of 15 years and has also been employed
at Danielmark’s as a bartender for the past 3 years. Amy, his wife of 15 years, is an English teacher in Cheyenne, and
together they have a ten-year-old daughter who loves life and playing hockey. Watching their child play at Danielmark’s
with other children has been wondrous for them, and continuing to foster this family atmosphere at the establishment for
their child to enjoy is highly important to them.
Richard Hart moved to Cheyenne in 2012 for his final assignment in the Air Force. For 20 years, Richard’s primary duties
were to repair and calibrate medical equipment. Richard’s girlfriend, Michelle, is the manager of the downtown Starbucks
location, who plans to dive in and assist with bartending and scheduling live music
If you have questions, please contact us at 301-312-9471. We look forward to meeting with all of you and doing our best to
be active and supportive community members and business owners in the city of Cheyenne.
Sincerely,
THE BLUE RAVEN BREWERY TEAM
Ryan Simeon Willson L t’t4-’
Kevin Louis Tighe
Richard Edward Hart
```

